===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[group]] of [[individual#Noun|individuals]] or [[company|companies]] formed to [[transact]] some specific [[business]], or to [[promote]] a common [[interest#Noun|interest]]; a self-[[coordinate#Verb|coordinating]] group.
#: {{ux|en|a gambling '''syndicate'''}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Julian Thomas|authorlink=Julian Thomas (journalist)|chapter=Maafu, Prince of Tonga|title=Cannibals & Convicts: Notes of Personal Experiences in the Western Pacific|location=London; New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Cassell (publisher)|Cassel & Company, Limited]]|year=1886|page=24|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=FlMWAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA24|oclc=780482546|passage=The worst deed ever alleged against the early sandalwood traders was that a number of natives were suffocated in a cave at Vaté, in the New Hebrides, by the smoke from a fire built at its mouth. But this was done by order of [[w:Enele Maʻafu|Maafu]], who, on behalf of an Australian '''syndicate''' of highly-respectable merchants and church-members, was "bossing" an expedition in search of sandalwood through the New Hebrides.}}
## {{lb|en|crime}} A group of [[gangster]]s engaged in [[organized crime]].
##* {{quote-book|author=John Madinger|chapter=Case Development|title=Confidential Informant: Law Enforcement’s Most Valuable Tool|location=Boca Raton, Fla.|publisher={{w|CRC Press}}|year=1999|page=178|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=aK1fo5LhgOYC&pg=PA178|isbn=978-0-8493-0709-6|passage=Held at the estate of Mafia boss [[w:Joseph Barbara (mobster)|Joseph Barbara]] in Apalachin, NY, the meeting called by [[w:Vito Genovese|[Vito] Genovese]] in November 1957 brought over 100 mobsters from around the country to cement his power over the national crime '''syndicate'''.}}
## {{lb|en|mass media}} A group of [[media]] companies, or an [[agency]], formed to [[acquire]] [[content#Noun|content]] such as [[article]]s, [[cartoon]]s, etc., and to [[publish]] it in [[multiple]] [[outlet]]s; a [[chain#Noun|chain]] of newspapers or other media outlets [[manage]]d by such an [[organization]].
# The [[office]] or [[jurisdiction]] of a [[syndic]]; a [[body]] or [[council]] of syndics.
#: {{rfquotek|Bishop Burnet}}
#* {{quote-journal|author=&#91;{{w|India Office}}, {{w|Government of the United Kingdom}}|chapter=Copy of Correspondence with the Indian Government, Showing the Progress of the Measures Adopted for Carrying Out the Education Despatch of the 19th Day of July 1854. [Bye-laws for the Government of the University of Madras.]|title=Accounts and Papers: Twenty-one Volumes. [...] Session 2, 31 May&nbsp;– 13 August 1859|location=[London|publisher=[[w:Office of Public Sector Information|Her Majesty's Stationery Office]]]|year=1859|volume=10 (East India (Education)), part II (Madras); volume XXIV, part II|page=367|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=LdISAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA367|oclc=380264703|passage=The executive government of the [[w:University of Madras|University [of Madras]]] shall be vested in a '''syndicate''', consisting of the Vice-Chancellor and six of the fellows, who shall be elected for one year by the several faculties, at the annual meetng of the senate, {{...}}}}

